overing-maps-among-complete-analytic-functions","thm-riemann-surface-of-the-logarithm","thm-riemann-surface-of-an-nth-root","rem-schwarz-reflection-as-analytic-continuation","def-singular-boundary-point-and-natural-boundary","thm-circle-of-convergence-contains-a-singular-point","thm-pringsheim-theorem","thm-factorial-gap-series-has-the-unit-circle-as-natural-boundary","ex-logarithm-continuation-around-the-unit-circle-shifts-by-two-pi-i","ex-square-root-continuation-around-the-origin-changes-sign","ex-helicoid-model-of-the-logarithm-surface","ex-two-sheeted-model-of-the-square-root-surface","ex-the-geometric-series-has-only-one-singular-boundary-point","cex-the-factorial-gap-series-has-the-unit-circle-as-a-natural-boundary","cex-sum-z-to-n-over-n-squared-is-continuous-on-the-closed-disc-but-singular-at-one","fs-every-holomorphic-function-on-a-domain-continues-past-its-boundary","fs-continuation-along-same-endpoint-paths-always-agrees","fs-the-riemann-surface-of-a-multivalued-function-is-always-a-subset-of-c-squared","fs-every-boundary-point-of-a-radius-one-power-series-is-singular"],"conventions":[{"convention":"$K_0(A,b)=\\{0\\}$; for $m\\ge1$, $K_m(A,b)=\\operatorname{span}\\{b,Ab,\\ldots,A^{m-1}b\\}$.","fixed_by":"def-krylov-subspace-of-a-matrix-and-start-vector","matters_for":["prop-krylov-subspace-is-the-polynomial-image-of-the-start-vector","thm-krylov-dimensions-grow-by-one-until-the-grade-and-then-stabilise","def-gmres-iterate"]},{"convention":"The relative minimal polynomial is monic of least degree annihilating $b$; for $b=0$ it is $1$ and the grade is $0$.","fixed_by":"def-grade-and-relative-minimal-polynomial-of-a-start-vector","matters_for":["thm-krylov-dimensions-grow-by-one-until-the-grade-and-then-stabilise","cor-for-invertible-a-the-exact-solution-enters-the-krylov-space-at-the-grade","thm-unrestarted-gmres-terminates-in-at-most-the-relative-grade-in-exact-arithmetic"]},{"convention":"All differentiation on complex matrix spaces is real Fréchet differentiation on their underlying real vector spaces, measured at the input by the Frobenius norm.","fixed_by":"def-real-frechet-derivative-on-real-and-complex-matrix-spaces","matters_for":["prop-matrix-differentials-obey-sum-product-and-adjoint-rules","thm-derivative-of-matrix-inversion","thm-directional-derivative-of-a-simple-positive-singular-value"]},{"convention":"The $L^p$ development uses real-valued measurable representatives; $L^p$ denotes their quotient by almost-everywhere equality.","fixed_by":"def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions","matters_for":["thm-the-l-p-norm-descends-to-the-quotient-and-makes-l-p-a-normed-space","thm-riesz-fischer-completeness-of-l-p","cor-l-p-convergence-implies-convergence-in-measure"]},{"convention":"For finite essential supremum, $\\|f\\|_\\infty$ is itself the least essential bound and the bound holds almost everywhere.","fixed_by":"prop-essential-supremum-is-attained-as-the-least-essential-bound","matters_for":["thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals","thm-minkowski-inequality-for-integrals","thm-l-p-norms-converge-to-the-essential-supremum-for-essentially-bounded-l-r-functions"]},{"convention":"An analytic-continuation chain begins with the specified germ and requires equality of successive germs at the path subdivision points.","fixed_by":"def-analytic-continuation-along-a-path","matters_for":["lem-refinement-of-analytic-continuation-chains","thm-end-germ-of-path-continuation-is-independent-of-the-chain","thm-monodromy-theorem"]},{"convention":"A complete analytic function is generated from a germ at $a_0$ under the hypothesis that continuation exists along every path in $\\Omega$ starting at $a_0$.","fixed_by":"def-complete-analytic-function","matters_for":["def-riemann-surface-of-a-complete-analytic-function","thm-riemann-surface-of-the-logarithm","thm-riemann-surface-of-an-nth-root"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals","statement":"For conjugate $p,q\\in[1,\\infty]$, $\\int|fg|\\,d\\mu\\le\\|f\\|_p\\|g\\|_q$, including the endpoint cases.","used_by":["thm-equality-case-in-holder-inequality","thm-generalized-holder-inequality-for-products","thm-minkowski-inequality-for-integrals"]},{"id":"thm-minkowski-inequality-for-integrals","statement":"For $1\\le p<\\infty$, $\\|f+g\\|_p\\le\\|f\\|_p+\\|g\\|_p$, and the analogous essential-supremum inequality holds in $L^\\infty$.","used_by":["thm-calligraphic-l-p-and-l-infinity-are-vector-spaces-for-p-at-least-one","thm-the-l-p-norm-descends-to-the-quotient-and-makes-l-p-a-normed-space","thm-riesz-fischer-completeness-of-l-p"]},{"id":"thm-riesz-fischer-completeness-of-l-p","statement":"$L^p(\\mu)$ is complete for $1\\le p\\le\\infty$, and a norm-convergent sequence has a subsequence of representatives converging almost everywhere.","used_by":["cor-l-p-convergent-sequences-have-almost-everywhere-convergent-subsequences","rem-lp-completeness-and-the-banach-property"]},{"id":"def-grade-and-relative-minimal-polynomial-of-a-start-vector","statement":"The grade $\\nu(A,b)$ is the degree of the monic relative minimal polynomial $q_{A,b}$ satisfying $q_{A,b}(A)b=0$.","used_by":["thm-krylov-dimensions-grow-by-one-until-the-grade-and-then-stabilise","cor-for-invertible-a-the-exact-solution-enters-the-krylov-space-at-the-grade","thm-unrestarted-gmres-terminates-in-at-most-the-relative-grade-in-exact-arithmetic"]},{"id":"thm-arnoldi-produces-an-orthonormal-krylov-basis-and-upper-hessenberg-factorization","statement":"Before breakdown, Arnoldi gives an orthonormal basis of $K_m(A,b)$ and $AQ_m=Q_{m+1}\\bar H_m$ with $\\bar H_m$ upper Hessenberg.","used_by":["prop-lucky-arnoldi-breakdown-is-equivalent-to-krylov-invariance","def-ritz-values-and-ritz-vectors-from-arnoldi","prop-ritz-residual-formula-for-an-arnoldi-ritz-pair","thm-arnoldi-reduces-gmres-to-a-small-hessenberg-least-squares-problem"]},{"id":"thm-simple-eigenpair-branches-exist-locally-after-gauge-fixing","statement":"A simple eigenvalue and a right eigenvector with $y_0^*x(A)=1$ admit unique local $C^1$ branches in the underlying real matrix space.","used_by":["thm-derivative-of-a-simple-eigenvalue-is-y-star-a-prime-x","thm-derivative-of-the-simple-spectral-projector","thm-gauge-fixed-simple-eigenvector-derivative-formula"]},{"id":"prop-reduced-resolvent-identities-for-a-simple-eigenvalue","statement":"The reduced resolvent satisfies $SP=PS=0$ and $S(A-\\lambda I)=(A-\\lambda I)S=I-P$.","used_by":["thm-derivative-of-the-simple-spectral-projector","thm-gauge-fixed-simple-eigenvector-derivative-formula"]},{"id":"def-analytic-continuation-along-a-path","statement":"An admissible chain of function elements along a path defines the terminal germ of pathwise continuation.","used_by":["lem-refinement-of-analytic-continuation-chains","thm-end-germ-of-path-continuation-is-independent-of-the-chain","thm-monodromy-theorem"]},{"id":"thm-monodromy-theorem","statement":"Fixed-endpoint homotopic paths give the same analytic continuation under continuation along every path from the initial germ.","used_by":["cor-single-valued-continuation-on-simply-connected-domains","rem-monodromy-corollary-agrees-with-the-earlier-simply-connected-logarithm-theorems"]},{"id":"lem-germ-neighborhoods-form-a-riemann-surface-basis","statement":"The germ neighborhoods form a Hausdorff, second-countable Riemann-surface atlas.","used_by":["thm-germ-projection-is-a-local-biholomorphism"]},{"id":"thm-factorial-gap-series-has-the-unit-circle-as-natural-boundary","statement":"$\\sum_{n\\ge0}z^{n!}$ has radius $1$ and the unit circle as a natural boundary.","used_by":["cex-the-factorial-gap-series-has-the-unit-circle-as-a-natural-boundary","fs-every-holomorphic-function-on-a-domain-continues-past-its-boundary"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"def-matrix-product-and-identity-matrix","used_for":"Matrix products in the Krylov, GMRES, and matrix-differential constructions.","opened":true},{"id":"def-inner-product-norm","used_for":"Arnoldi normalization and orthogonality.","opened":true},{"id":"def-upper-hessenberg-and-real-symmetric-tridiagonal-matrices","used_for":"The Arnoldi Hessenberg factorization.","opened":true},{"id":"def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum","used_for":"Ritz data and simple-eigenvalue terminology.","opened":true},{"id":"def-invertible-matrix-and-general-linear-group","used_for":"Krylov exact-solution and matrix-inversion assertions.","opened":true},{"id":"def-frobenius-matrix-norm","used_for":"The real Fréchet derivative convention.","opened":true},{"id":"def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism","used_for":"Hermitian eigenpair simplifications.","opened":true},{"id":"def-measure-space","used_for":"The ambient measure-space convention throughout the $L^p$ page.","opened":true},{"id":"def-measure-null-set-and-almost-everywhere","used_for":"Essential bounds, null functions, and quotienting by almost-everywhere equality.","opened":true},{"id":"def-nonnegative-lebesgue-integral","used_for":"The $p$-functional and integral inequalities.","opened":true},{"id":"prop-order-and-scalar-rules-for-the-nonnegative-integral","used_for":"Integral monotonicity and homogeneity in the $L^p$ arguments.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-additivity-of-the-nonnegative-lebesgue-integral","used_for":"Additivity of the nonnegative integral in the $L^p$ arguments.","opened":true},{"id":"def-real-power","used_for":"The real-exponent convention in the $L^p$ functional and power examples.","opened":true},{"id":"def-complex-differentiability-holomorphic-and-entire","used_for":"Holomorphic germs and function elements.","opened":true},{"id":"def-complex-domain","used_for":"Domains of function elements and analytic continuation.","opened":true},{"id":"def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy","used_for":"Endpoint-fixed path homotopies in monodromy.","opened":true},{"id":"def-simply-connected","used_for":"The simply-connected monodromy corollary.","opened":true},{"id":"def-biholomorphic-map","used_for":"The local-biholomorphism conclusion for the germ projection.","opened":true},{"id":"def-covering-map-and-evenly-covered-neighbourhoods","used_for":"The distinction between local biholomorphisms and covering maps.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-algebra-of-complex-derivatives","used_for":"The reciprocal-germ argument in the local-ring theorem.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-basis-criterion","used_for":"The germ-neighborhood topology.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-cauchy-hadamard-for-complex-power-series","used_for":"The circle-of-convergence and boundary examples.","opened":true},{"id":"def-factorial-and-falling-factorial","used_for":"Factorial divisibility in the gap-series argument.","opened":true}],"concerns":[{"id":"def-real-frechet-derivative-on-real-and-complex-matrix-spaces","concern":"It gives the codomain as an arbitrary finite-dimensional real vector space $W$ but supplies no norm on $W$, so the vector-valued term $o(\\|H\\|_F)$ is undefined.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-grade-and-relative-minimal-polynomial-of-a-start-vector","concern":"It asserts existence and uniqueness of the monic least-degree annihilating polynomial with no supporting dependency or derivation. This well-definedness is used throughout the Krylov chain.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"prop-krylov-subspace-is-the-polynomial-image-of-the-start-vector","concern":"Its set is quantified by $\\deg p<m$, but neither the statement nor its dependencies assign a degree to the zero polynomial. Step 1.1 may construct $p=0$, so the claimed equality is not well-formed at $v=0$.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-arnoldi-produces-an-orthonormal-krylov-basis-and-upper-hessenberg-factorization","concern":"The definition supplies $h_{ij}$ only for $i\\le j$ plus $h_{j+1,j}$, whereas $\\bar H_m=(h_{ij})_{1\\le i\\le m+1,1\\le j\\le m}$ uses entries with $i>j+1$ without defining them as zero.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"prop-lucky-arnoldi-breakdown-is-equivalent-to-krylov-invariance","concern":"The statement omits $m\\ge1$. At $m=0$, $h_{1,0}$ and the claimed next Arnoldi residual are undefined.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-calligraphic-l-p-on-a-measure-space","concern":"For a measurable function with $\\int|f|^p\\,d\\mu=\\infty$, it writes $(\\infty)^{1/p}$ although its cited real-power convention defines powers only for positive finite bases and zero.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"rem-finite-counting-measure-holder-and-cauchy-schwarz-agree-with-published-finite-inequalities","concern":"The integral Cauchy--Schwarz specialization is $\\sum_k|x_ky_k|\\le\\|x\\|_2\\|y\\|_2$, whereas the ordinary finite Cauchy--Schwarz statement is $|\\sum_kx_ky_k|\\le\\|x\\|_2\\|y\\|_2$; the remark's claimed direct agreement is false.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"def-compatible-left-and-right-eigenvectors-for-a-simple-eigenvalue","concern":"It does not restrict $A$ to a real or complex matrix space or specify an adjoint structure, while it uses $A^*$ and $\\overline\\lambda$.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-monodromy-theorem","concern":"It assumes continuation along paths starting at $a_0$ but states only that $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ have the same endpoints; it never requires their common initial point to be $a_0$, so the stated continuations may be undefined.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"ex-a-two-step-function-shows-the-l-p-norm-converging-to-the-essential-supremum","concern":"Step 2.1 factors the norm correctly as $2(1/2+2^{-p-1})^{1/p}$ but then says “The bracket tends to $1$”; the bracket tends to $1/2$ (its $p$th root tends to $1$).","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-factorial-gap-series-has-the-unit-circle-as-natural-boundary","concern":"Step 1.1 says the coefficients are “1 at the factorial indices,” but $0!=1!=1$, so the coefficient of $z^1$ is $2$. The radius and natural-boundary conclusion are unaffected.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"lem-refinement-of-analytic-continuation-chains","concern":"Step 2.1 calls restrictions of function elements to parameter subintervals a refinement, although function elements are defined on complex domains. The asserted choice also does not explain preservation of the chain's joining-germ conditions.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-end-germ-of-path-continuation-is-independent-of-the-chain","concern":"Step 2.1 invokes the identity theorem on a connected component of $U_k\\cap V_k$ without establishing that this component is open and hence a complex domain.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-determinant-differential-and-jacobis-formula","concern":"The Jacobi specialization uses $\\operatorname{adj}(A)=\\det(A)A^{-1}$ but no cited fact supplies that identity.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals","concern":"Its endpoint proof passes from an almost-everywhere inequality $|fg|\\le M|f|$ to an integral inequality without citing an a.e.-invariance or a.e.-monotonicity result for the nonnegative integral.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-minkowski-inequality-for-integrals","concern":"The proof uses integrals of $|f+g|^p$ and concludes $f+g\\in\\mathcal L^p$ without citing or deriving that $f+g$ is measurable.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-riemann-surface-of-the-logarithm","concern":"In step 1.2, the conditions $|(t_{j+1}-t_j)w|<1/2$ and $|\\operatorname{Im}((t_{j+1}-t_j)w)|<\\pi$ do not by themselves show that the stated radius-$1/2$ branch neighborhoods overlap at the joining point; a stronger smallness condition on $|e^{(t_{j+1}-t_j)w}-1|$ is needed.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}